{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"content","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLSlashContentV","text":"MXLSlashContent","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlashContent"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlash\/content","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The slash group combines elements used for more complete specification of the slash and beat-repeat measure-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"style elements. They have the same values as the type and dot elements, and define what the beat is for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display of repetition marks. If not present, the beat is based on the current time signature."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslash\/content"]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"content","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLSlashContentV","text":"MXLSlashContent","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSlashV7contentAA0C7ContentVSgvp","role":"symbol","title":"content"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlash"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSlash/content":{"abstract":[{"text":"The slash group combines elements used for more complete specification of the slash and beat-repeat measure-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"style elements. They have the same values as the type and dot elements, and define what the beat is for the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display of repetition marks. If not present, the beat is based on the current time signature."}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"content","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSlashContent","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLSlashContentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"content","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslash\/content","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlash\/content"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSlashContent":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLSlashContent","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSlashContent","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslashcontent","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlashContent","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSlashContent","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The slash group combines elements used for more complete specification of the slash and beat-repeat measure-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"style elements. They have the same values as the type and dot elements, and define what the beat is for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display of repetition marks. If not present, the beat is based on the current time signature."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSlash":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslash","title":"MXLSlash","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSlash","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSlash","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The slash type is used to indicate that slash notation is to be used. If the slash is on every beat, use-stems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is no (the default). To indicate rhythms but not pitches, use-stems is set to yes. The type attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates whether this is the start or stop of a slash notation style. The use-dots attribute works as for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"beat-repeat element, and only has effect if use-stems is no."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlash"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}